<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5"><strong>Key Arch=
itectural Decisions for Financial Precision:</strong></h2>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Use BigInt for integer =
storage</strong> - Avoid floating-point entirely for monetary values</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Decimal.js in Workers</=
strong> - For exact decimal arithmetic in calculations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Audit trail generation<=
/strong> - Every calculation step recorded for regulatory compliance</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Data integrity hashing<=
/strong> - Detect any data corruption during transfer</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Currency-aware serializ=
ation</strong> - Handle multi-currency scenarios properly</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The trade-off here is pe=
rformance vs. precision</strong>: The Decimal.js approach is slower but mat=
hematically exact, while the BigInt approach is faster but requires careful=
 handling of the conversion multipliers.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">For a bank like NAB, I'd recomme=
nd the <strong>hybrid approach</strong>: use BigInt serialization for data =
transfer efficiency, but convert to Decimal.js objects in workers for actua=
l financial calculations.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent! Your attention to regulatory compliance and data integrity is exac=
tly what we look for. Now, let's dive into some potential edge cases. What =
happens when you're transferring a 15MB ArrayBuffer to a Web Worker, but th=
e user's device has limited memory? How would you handle memory pressure sc=
enarios, and what fallback strategies would you implement?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's a critical production concern! <strong>Memory pressure is especially imp=
ortant in banking applications</strong> where users might have multiple bro=
wser tabs open with trading platforms, and memory leaks could impact tradin=
g decisions. Let me outline a comprehensive memory management strategy:</p>
