<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5"><strong>Key Mult=
i-Currency Design Principles:</strong></h2>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5"><strong>1. Curre=
ncy-Specific Precision Configuration</strong></h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Each currency has its own precis=
ion rules, rounding behavior, and regulatory requirements. JPY rounds to in=
tegers, USD to cents, BTC to 8 decimals.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5"><strong>2. Seque=
ntial Precision Application</strong></h3>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Calculate</strong> in n=
ative currency first</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Round</strong> to nativ=
e currency precision</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Convert</strong> to bas=
e currency</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Round</strong> to base =
currency precision</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This prevents <strong>cascading =
rounding errors</strong> that could accumulate across conversions.</p>
