<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5"><strong>Performa=
nce Expectations</strong></h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">With this architecture:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Throughput</strong>: 2M=
+ messages/minute sustained</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Latency</strong>: &lt;5=
0ms end-to-end during peak load</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory</strong>: Linear=
 scaling with subscriber count</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>CPU</strong>: Auto-scal=
ing prevents saturation</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Reliability</strong>: G=
raceful degradation, no data loss</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is <strong>separ=
ating concerns</strong>: parsing workers handle raw data, calculation worke=
rs do financial math, and aggregation workers handle trader distribution. T=
his <strong>pipeline architecture</strong> prevents any single bottleneck f=
rom affecting the entire system.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding! Your enterprise scaling approach shows deep understanding of rea=
l-world trading system requirements. For my final question, let's talk abou=
t observability and debugging. In a production environment with this comple=
xity, how would you implement comprehensive monitoring and debugging capabi=
lities? Specifically, if a trader reports that their EUR/USD moving average=
s seem "off" during a particular 5-minute window last Tuesday, how would yo=
u investigate this?</p>
<hr>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5"><strong>Part 4: =
Production Observability &amp; Debugging</strong></h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's an excellent production scenario! <strong>"EUR/USD moving averages seem =
off"</strong> is the kind of vague but critical issue that requires <strong=
>forensic-level observability</strong>. In trading systems, data accuracy i=
sn't just about user experience - it could be the difference between profit=
 and significant losses, or even regulatory violations.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me design a comprehensive ob=
servability system:</p>
